{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31964 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Colenemol is implicated in the interaction with FaDu through a series of molecular targets that ultimately converge on the same cellular pathway. The evidence suggests that Colenemol acts as a target for multiple compounds, including N,3,5,8-Tetrabromo-6-(Bromomethyl)Naphthalen-2-Amine, 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, and Javanicoside F, all of which are known to target the Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is a key player in the signaling cascade that leads to the activation of FaDu, indicating a potential mechanism by which Colenemol influences cellular processes in this cell line. The shared target of these compounds, coupled with the direct interaction with FaDu, suggests a possible role in modulating cellular responses, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
